# Southampton Refine — new thread over junk context

Site memory lives in `site/` files (`QUEUE.txt`, `PROCESS.txt`, place briefs,
`ISSUES.txt`), not in chat history. Accuracy only — no fictional districts.

Before doing a new queue item or live-world build in this conversation:

1. If this thread already finished a queue item (lock released / QUEUE marked
   done), or is dominated by prior build/debug, **do not silently continue**.
2. Tell the user briefly that a **new chat** would be wiser, and point them at
   `python3 scripts/site_handoff.py next` (also refreshes `site/HANDOFF.txt`).
3. Only stay in-thread for a short same-item follow-up (e.g. one patrol fix
   right after a build they just asked for here).

When finishing a queue item: `python3 scripts/site_handoff.py end Q-nnn` after
releasing the lock. Do not ask the user to paste long prior-chat summaries.
